  ('en', 'usage.jev.work.answerRecalled', $json$"Earlier answers reused"$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.projectNotes.title', $json$"Project memory"$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.projectNotes.detail', $json$"On a project's chats screen, the Project memory button keeps short notes (up to 2,200 characters): how to test, where things live, what not to touch. They go to the agent once, when the session starts, and spare it from exploring the project to find them again. Secrets are refused, and everything syncs with your account."$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.gateLearning.title', $json$"The gatehouse learns from your answers"$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.gateLearning.detail', $json$"When the gatehouse asks where something lives or how to check a change and you answer in your next request, the sentence that answered becomes a project note. From then on the gatehouse no longer asks that in the project, and the agent already gets the answer."$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.routingFeedback.title', $json$"Routing learns from what did not work"$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.routingFeedback.detail', $json$"An answer that arrived whole no longer always counts as a success. If your next message says it did not work, or the exit gate holds the answer, the model that answered loses a point. Each model's score is now also kept per kind of request, so reviews and tests can go to different models."$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.levelSuggestion.title', $json$"Level suggestion"$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.levelSuggestion.detail', $json$"In Settings, Your level now suggests moving one step up or down when the gatehouse history of the last 30 days calls for it (from 20 requests on): almost everything getting through at once, or many requests held. The switch is still yours, with one click."$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.chatSearch.title', $json$"Search your chats"$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.chatSearch.detail', $json$"A project's chats screen now has a search over what was said in its chats, with the matching passage highlighted. It runs on your computer, on a local index, without going to the network."$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.answerRecall.title', $json$"Reuses answers the project already has"$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.answerRecall.detail', $json$"When a request is nearly identical to one already answered in another chat of the same project, the earlier answer goes along, shortened, and the agent starts from it instead of exploring and answering everything again. Each time this happens shows up in the Jev panel."$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.recipes.title', $json$"Recipes for requests you repeat"$json$::jsonb),
  ('en', 'whatsNew.item.recipes.detail', $json$"Project memory shows the requests you have made three or more times and lets you turn them into a recipe: your procedure for that kind of request. The recipe goes along only when a request looks like it, so it adds nothing to the others."$json$::jsonb),
